  "note": "Third and fourth seeds for the position-profile slopes. Two seeds established that the\nfp8 slope changes sign between them and that a within-run cluster bootstrap CI does not\ncapture that variation, which forced the withdrawal of a single-seed 'quantisation flips the\nsign' conclusion. Two seeds can show that an interval is too narrow but cannot estimate how\nwide the truth is: with n=2 the seed-level standard error is itself a one-degree-of-freedom\nquantity.\n\nFour seeds make the across-seed spread reportable, which is what the honest version of this\nresult needs: a slope with an interval that actually reflects seed variation, rather than\n'not detectable' backed by two points. The bf16 arm is included as the control that has been\nstable so far (-3.21e-07, -3.76e-07) -- if it stays stable while fp8 keeps scattering, that\ncontrast is itself the finding.",
